+# Matched portable receiver control on DS26-0162
+
+Test passive self-location from the complete signed recording DS26-0162, selected by the experiment roster in advance. The signed manifests identify its pilot edge as upper. Run the ordinary portable command at revision `18cb0f7c8` and the compact-kernel option through the public command. Use the original 10 MHz dual CI16 recording, physical capture validator, acquisition schedule, track configuration, frozen position offer and causally selected TLEs. Earlier nested-anchor and portable studies provide context. Publish only fresh position results from the scheduled raw runs. An independent compact fit from the archived original-schedule measured GLRT factors serves as the position and factor control.
+
+Use the same one-worker-per-core assignment on CPUs 0–7, with 600 seconds per raw worker and 180 seconds for the two-arm position service. The ordinary command runs first. Record per-worker and whole-command wall and CPU, acquisition and verification CPU, per-visit wall and CPU quantiles, signed timeline, valid and excluded visits, and charged memory. Account for authenticated closed chunks even when a worker reaches a deadline. Capture serving load and affinity. The full runs occur at different times on a shared host. Treat any alternated matched-chunk timing as a separate diagnostic.
+
+Require terminal records for ordinary portable, compact kernels, archived compact and all four original v5 roles. Verify signed visits, exclusions, clocks, selected causal snapshot, ordered probe keys and gates. Compare candidate counts, positional ranks, each candidate field, and circular CFO using the prior archived physical match tolerance at 0.5 sample and 250 Hz. Audit the earliest changed probe and the first macroscopic support, rank or gate difference when present. Seal predictions and bindings before opening survey labels.
+
+Both calibration arms share measured factors, causal TLEs, priors and search budgets within each receiver. Score geographic error in kilometres and report CFO residual RMS in hertz and available objectives separately. Evaluate each arm against all v5 roles at 5% and 10% relative degradation. Both arms must publish to meet a paired target. Preserve unavailable outcomes, including timeouts, without replacing them with archived or forced endpoints. Use the prior release's position figure schema v2 and stage schema v1, with all plotted points and aggregates in the CSVs.
