+# Collapse repeated orbit interpolation in compact v5
+
+The installed compact lifetime receiver projects a center orbit state and two neighboring phase states for every satellite and observation. The candidate computes the center as before. If the two neighbors use the same knot pair, it computes their centered difference from the mean rotation and the change in rotation. If the neighbors straddle a knot, it computes both neighboring states with the installed arithmetic. The mechanism does not retain projections across calls. The installed preparation, fits and joint publication run in their ordinary order with both calibration arms. The experiment starts at recorded native GLRT and excludes IQ decoding and detection.
+
+Select one original DS26 offer and one original DS29 offer by sorting eligible first-segment manifest digests with the `compact-secant-20261120` salt. Eligibility requires complete authenticated capture-era native factors, track configuration, and causal element snapshots. Exclude the earlier checksum and track-preparation panels and the DS26-0102 near-omission control. Include that existing shifted control as a third offer with the same center and publication gate as its sealed earlier run. Freeze all case bindings and package and candidate digests before launching any positions. Open geographic references only after sealing terminal predictions and resource receipts. Show the four original v5 reference roles where the offer and archived inputs match.
+
+Run each pair on the same pinned CPU, in counterbalanced order across CPUs 14 and 15, with one numerical thread, 512 MiB memory, zero swap, and a 180-second service limit. Include candidate compilation, causal preparation, inference, and output in service clocks. Count original projection calls and cells, same-interval cells, and projection CPU. Retain every terminal outcome. A candidate passes numerical parity when paired decisions match, endpoints shift at most 20 m, conditional RF RMS changes by at most 0.01 Hz and frequency objectives change by at most 0.1 when present. The projector tests require identical Doppler and elevation and a 1e-6 Hz/s absolute secant tolerance on supported GNSS-like state magnitudes. Require at least 5% median paired full-service CPU reduction for a material improvement and report the paired wall and memory independently. A timeout or publication change fails parity in that pair. Report position error and RF effects for zero and fitted calibration separately.
