+# Shared receiver clock and Doppler alias qualification
+
+Estimate passive receiver location from stored GLRT winners and a causal TLE catalogue within the originally supplied 25 km tile. Measure the complete route from authenticated GLRT and capture configuration to both calibration fits. The numerical worker receives no reference endpoint, receiver truth, V5 observation, or fitted orbit. Start each location fit at the supplied tile centre, with WGS84 sea-level altitude.
+
+The original joint worker searches candidate pairs and shares a per-orbit timing displacement. Track quadrature changes the cost of its shortlist only. Trackless differences discard absolute levels and showed weak geographic evidence. The original marginal-offset fit applies one Gaussian level prior to every track. The original shared-clock fit adds 22 shared Gaussian time columns to the original assignments. This experiment tests a smaller receiver clock with a conditional absolute-Doppler constraint. It uses one anonymous nomination for both test and control and analytically profiles each track constant. An absolute Doppler constraint enters when two disjoint time halves agree on a single 227,272.727 Hz alias and their estimated residual levels are consistent. Offsets on the remaining tracks are free. Each physical receiver shares a fractional-frequency trend across its tunings with separate group intercepts. Each nominated orbit shares one timing displacement. Keep all aliases, orbit assignments, points, and budgets fixed for the paired c fits.
+
+Select the first two digest-ranked recordings per dataset for development and the next three per dataset for the held panel. Rank by SHA-256 of the literal `direct-clock-20261120-v1:` followed by the native archive digest. Eligibility requires a frozen positive anonymous track census and the original catalogue and tile binding. Development can inspect clock, residual and support diagnostics. It cannot inspect geographic errors. Freeze thresholds and source hashes before launching held work. An extra query for the first held DS26 recording moves the tile 50 km east of the original centre, using the same dimensions, capture and catalogue. Confirm the omission after the prediction seal. Repeat the held ordinary offers with each orbital timestamp shifted 73 s, keeping measured time, sample order, offered tile, and causal element selection fixed. Report withheld, timed out, forced, and published endpoints separately.
+
+Compare the constrained method to free track constants with identical nomination and to the original native joint worker. The free constants absorb the fixed-RF calibration exactly. Run the numerical fit in both calibration configurations and mark the coefficient unidentifiable. Hold out synchronized whole-track time blocks and predict the second half of each test track after using its first half to resolve the discrete ambiguity. Report the held frequency residual and the conditional fit separately from location accuracy. Authenticate the four original V5 variants for each ordinary capture and tile.
+
+Run one numerical thread on CPU 12 or 13 with 512 MiB virtual-memory limit and a 90 s timeout per attempt. Alternate pair order on each core. Touch only capture data already on disk. Record CPU and wall time for archive reading, Graph, orbit setup, candidate screening, nomination, and the final numerical fits, plus projection, candidate, and fit counts. The geographic criterion is full V5 publication coverage and a median and P95 within 10% of every available original V5 role for both c configurations. The paired cost criterion is lower measured process CPU than the freshly rerun native joint receiver, with unchanged input support before fitting. Time IQ processing separately from this experiment.
