+# Combined C kernel qualification
+
+The experiment tests whether the shared Qin phase-pair bank and compact CI16 verifier reduce resident stereo detector CPU and workspace while preserving the field output. It uses the existing field ABI and saved complex int16 samples. The control is the portable field shared library compiled from the as-run source closure before changes. The candidate is the direct build with the same optimization flags and host architecture.
+
+The held panel is the prior verifier-memory panel from the signed original-schedule verifier-integration receipt. It has four visits per producer from DS26-0237, DS29-0082 and DS29-0519. They span both edges and include rejected, dilute, equivalent and stereo-positive cases. Compare all groups and ranks, including the superseded primary group when a peer retry runs. Require exact lane, anchor, count, candidate epoch and seed identity, tie/gate flags and null state. For physical values use absolute bounds of 1 Hz for CFO, 2 × 10⁻⁹ sample for fractional offsets and 10⁻⁵ for scores, with actual maxima recorded. The prior field tolerances bound coarse float32 drift. The two kernels must also reproduce zero IQ and invalid field ABI behavior. Retained-seed sentinels from the earlier qualification cover closer ties and the fractional gate boundary when applicable.
+
+Pin two fresh, sequential native processes to CPU 8 or 9 in each of six interleaved pairs, balancing arm order on each CPU. Hold compiler, Python, input bytes, edge, CFO bounds and process structure constant. Stage inputs on the local bulk volume before timing, with scratch on the same volume. Time the resident detector calls and record full process CPU and elapsed time, kernel stage clocks, native high-water RSS, workspace bytes, shared-library sections, and input/output counts. Report medians and paired spread. Use the prior profiling results to contextualize the measured stage clocks. Interpret improvement only when paired reductions exceed variability and all inventory/numerical gates pass. Stage results alone establish neither location accuracy nor embedded throughput.
