+# Public replay command verification
+
+Exercise the default `tools.pipeline_eval.portable_receiver` public command with a SHA-256 authenticated DS29-0082 locator. Use the same first signed chunk as the promoted command's previous locator smoke. DS29-0082 is a saved upper-edge dual CI16 recording. The locator contains the signed recording manifests, no-repair request, search region, session and run identities. The request supplies the causal catalogue and receiver configuration. The locator has no archived factor entry. Keep truth unavailable to prediction and leave the archive read-only.
+
+Use `--smoke --cpus 18 --raw-limit 600 --position-limit 180`. Pin the command supervisor to CPU 18 and set its scratch beneath `/srv/bulk/leo-dev/direct-receiver-20261120/public-route`. Use the usual single-core service with a 512 MiB charge limit and zero swap. Take one throughput observation on the shared host. No speed ranking follows from this smoke.
+
+Require exactly one authenticated complete chunk, identical scheduled and completed visit counts, a successful service receipt with a matching CPU and source lock, and no native or position handoff. Compare detector coverage and group count to the existing sealed locator smoke. Compare historical and current numeric identity when the build warrants that claim. Preserve the whole-command clock, worker CPU and memory, per-visit detector time, signed chunk identity, source lock and compact terminal evidence. Seal the input before executing and keep the run seal and source hashes.
+
+Exercise both public flags, sha rejection, timeout before position, detached-module reconciliation, and archive-interpreter imports with hermetic tests. Attribute scientific performance of compact kernels to their own sealed field comparison. Position endpoints, geographic error and the `c` ablation are outside the one-chunk smoke boundary.
