+# Streaming fixed-point Qin coarse acquisition protocol
+
+## Decision and scope
+
+Test whether fixed-point rolling correlation and anchor folding retain coarse acquisition and GLRT decisions and fit the 20 ms dual-radio visit budget. Time the normal standalone C detector from resident CI16 through seed selection, fine search, fractional GLRT and conditional retry. Keep the decoder, production gate and fine verifier fixed. The study produces detector measurements and does not compute receiver positions.
+
+The original deployed-shaped search spans 21 residual CFO hypotheses at 80 kHz spacing through ±800 kHz on each physical lane. Each visit has 200,000 stereo samples at 10 MS/s. Both 12- and 22-anchor masks, 44 taps, exact integer frame origins, and 13,333 epochs remain in the work count. The independent cell oracle directly evaluates known complex pilots over finite 44-sample windows. The incumbent also supplies a full-grid and downstream comparison.
+
+## Inputs and acceptance
+
+Use the existing authenticated `c-coarse-tiles-panel-v2` inputs. Freeze the three recording IDs DS26-0237, DS29-0082, and DS29-0519, each historical and manifest-hash held file, and the prior controls. Resolve their hashes from the published coarse-tiles input evidence before execution. The held visits were selected before this mechanism. Use the three development visits only for implementation checks. Run both anchors on physical held lanes, and preserve the real peer-retry rules in the separate verifier run. No TLE, site coordinates, reference scores, or historical candidate labels enter detection.
+
+Compare ordered seeds, original and refined epochs, support, cell scores, and downstream ordered candidates and fractional gates. Publish every discrepancy and the nearest positive and negative gate distances. Select direct cell probes at deterministic internals, time bounds, CFO bounds, and leading peaks from the incumbent. Include exact synthetic selector ties, masked and truncated captures, zero and time-reversed IQ, and full-width full-scale arithmetic. Use a 5 × 10⁻⁵ absolute score tolerance for the direct cell oracle and require the same peak keys and downstream gates for a parity claim. Avoid changing the fixed-point scale based on held outcomes.
+
+Use CPU 10 and CPU 11 only. Build optimized x86 and Cortex-A9 binaries, run a small Cortex-A9 correctness stream under QEMU, and record its results separately. Alternate baseline and candidate timings on full held CI16. Record CPU and wall clocks, work counters, source and ELF footprint, and a one-sample/cycle hardware schedule with explicit drains and an optional sink stall. Hardware clocks and resources are bounds and extrapolations. A complete software detector exceeding 20 ms, or a chosen hardware schedule exhausting the device's gross resources before fine verification, rules out that implementation for the board. Use local bulk scratch only.
+
+## Execution dependencies
+
+- Authenticate archive inputs and compile the normal entry point before timing.
+- Run real CI16 and hermetic tests from the same instrumented math. Keep them in distinct output directories.
+- Keep report writes local to this stage. The qualification run owns those artifacts once it has completed all comparisons.
+- A single worker owns this tightly coupled kernel, fixture and evidence. Delegation is disabled by the receiver brief.
